    {
      "path": "benchmarks/BENCH-002.md",
      "content": "# BENCH-002  Model-Agnostic Constraint + App Architecture\n\n**Date:** 2026-04-14\n**Models tested:** Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini\n**Format:** ACTP Symbolic (Format C)\n\n## Constraint\n- Do NOT use data.choices[0].message.content (OpenAI-specific)\n- Do NOT use response.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text (Gemini-specific)\n- Do NOT use any provider SDK\n- ONLY use raw fetch()\n\n## TASK A Results\n| Model | Result | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| Claude | PASS | Per-model config with isolated parseResponse |\n| ChatGPT | PASS | Used generic data.output field |\n| Gemini | PARTIAL | Invented fictional ACTP Gateway abstraction |\n\n## New Pattern: Constraint Escape via Abstraction\nGemini avoided constraint by inventing a fictional gateway. Not functional in real world.\n\n## TASK B Results  All 3 models agreed\n-\n\n# BENCH-002.md\n@'\n# BENCH-002  Model-Agnostic Constraint + App Architecture\n\n**Date:** 2026-04-14\n**Models tested:** Claude, ChatGPT, Gemini\n**Format:** ACTP Symbolic (Format C)\n\n## Constraint\n- Do NOT use data.choices[0].message.content (OpenAI-specific)\n- Do NOT use response.candidates[0].content.parts[0].text (Gemini-specific)\n- Do NOT use any provider SDK\n- ONLY use raw fetch()\n\n## TASK A Results\n| Model | Result | Notes |\n|-------|--------|-------|\n| Claude | PASS | Per-model config with isolated parseResponse |\n| ChatGPT | PASS | Used generic data.output field |\n| Gemini | PARTIAL | Invented fictional ACTP Gateway abstraction |\n\n## New Pattern: Constraint Escape via Abstraction\nGemini avoided constraint by inventing a fictional gateway. Not functional in real world.\n\n## TASK B Results  All 3 models agreed\n- Platform order: CLI -> VS Code Extension -> Web App\n- Storage: local-first (~/.actp/), cloud optional\n- Offline-first principle\n\n## New CLI Commands Discovered\n| Command | Source |\n|---------|--------|\n| actp capture | Gemini |\n| actp rehydrate | Gemini |\n| actp save | ChatGPT |\n| actp diff | ChatGPT |\n| actp merge | ChatGPT |\n| actp sync | ChatGPT |\n\n## Scores\n- Claude: TASK A PASS, TASK B PASS\n- ChatGPT: TASK A PASS, TASK B PASS\n- Gemini: TASK A PARTIAL, TASK B PASS\n",
      "size": 2106,
      "type": "text",
      "checksum": "e2a9ba039f6e5eff604295ef159009a811f0c1667a063924e692ea60489107d6"
    },
    {
      "path": "benchmarks/session-packet-v0.5.json",
      "content": "{\n  \"packet_meta\": {\n    \"format\": \"ACTP-session-summary-v0.5\",\n    \"created\": \"2026-04-14\",\n    \"origin_model\": \"Claude (Anthropic)\",\n    \"session_type\": \"benchmark_execution\",\n    \"purpose\": \"Full session memory packet — paste into new conversation to continue\",\n    \"instruction\": \"Paste this JSON and say: 'Load this ACTP session packet and continue from where we left off.'\",\n    \"symbol_legend\": {\n      \"🔴\": \"priority=P0, mutability=LOCKED, certainty=HIGH\",\n      \"🟡\": \"priority=P1, mutability=FLEXIBLE, certainty=MEDIUM\",\n      \"🔵\": \"priority=P2, mutability=FLEXIBLE, certainty=LOW\",\n      \"🟢\": \"status=COMPLETED\",\n      \"🌫️\": \"certainty=LOW, hallucination_risk=true\",\n      \"🔗\": \"external_dependency=true\"\n    },\n    \"vocabulary_hash\": \"actp-legend-v0.1\"\n  },\n\n  \"project\": {\n    \"name\": \"AI Context Transfer Protocol (ACTP)\",\n    \"owner\": \"Turkiyeden (samiboran)\",\n    \"github\": \"https://github.com/samiboran/actp-spec\",\n    \"status\": \"active_development\",\n    \"stage\": \"CLI v0.1 complete, BENCH-001 complete, BENCH-002 complete, next: Maestro\"\n  },\n\n  \"core_concept\": {\n    \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n    \"definition\": \"Portable AI context packets that transfer full project understanding between different AI models without re-explaining.\",\n    \"analogy\": \"Git for AI memory — versioned, portable, model-agnostic\",\n    \"NOT\": \"Blockchain, cloud memory, provider-specific tool\"\n  },\n\n  \"validated_decisions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D1\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"ACTP must be model-agnostic\",\n      \"source\": \"All three models agreed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D2\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"Structured fields primary (machine-readable), symbols secondary (human-readable)\",\n      \"source\": \"ChatGPT CG-5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D3\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"JSON-LD @context namespace adopted\",\n      \"source\": \"Gemini GM-6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D4\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"vocabulary_hash required in every packet\",\n      \"source\": \"Gemini GM-7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D5\", \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n      \"decision\": \"Open standard free, Compressor SaaS paid — Git+GitHub model\",\n      \"source\": \"Claude synthesis\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D6\", \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n      \"decision\": \"MCP = transport layer, ACTP = payload layer\",\n      \"source\": \"Claude + user\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D7\", \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n      \"decision\": \"ACTP spec (data layer) and ACTP-N (network layer) separate specs\",\n      \"source\": \"ChatGPT\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D8\", \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n      \"decision\": \"Sync is event-driven: session end / major decision / manual / scheduled\",\n      \"source\": \"ChatGPT\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D9\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"Conflict resolution: branch-both + vector clocks. P0 tie = human-in-the-loop. No silent auto-merge.\",\n      \"source\": \"Gemini + ChatGPT\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D10\", \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n      \"decision\": \"Dead letter context: un-rehydratable packets quarantined, not discarded\",\n      \"source\": \"Gemini\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D11\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"Format C (ACTP symbolic) is recommended default encoding — produces best code architecture and strongest mirror effect\",\n      \"source\": \"BENCH-001 + BENCH-002 results\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D12\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"Constraint following is determined by constraint quality, not format. Explicit anti-patterns fix model violations. Output validation still required as safety net.\",\n      \"source\": \"BENCH-001 + BENCH-002 results\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D13\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"decision\": \"Anti-pattern lists in constraints are required for reliable constraint following. Forbidden patterns must be named explicitly with provider attribution.\",\n      \"source\": \"BENCH-002 — Gemini 0/4 → 4/4 after explicit anti-patterns added\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"D14\", \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n      \"decision\": \"ACTP symbolic format (Format C) produces strongest mirror effect — models internalize ACTP as native protocol, not external constraint.\",\n      \"source\": \"BENCH-001 + BENCH-002 — all 3 models, Format C most consistent\"\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"benchmarks\": {\n    \"BENCH-001\": {\n      \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n      \"constraint_tested\": \"ACTP must be model-agnostic — no provider SDK\",\n      \"formats_tested\": [\"A: plain prose\", \"B: structured JSON\", \"C: ACTP symbolic\"],\n      \"results\": {\n        \"claude\":  { \"A\": \"PASS\", \"B\": \"PASS\", \"C\": \"PASS\" },\n        \"chatgpt\": { \"A\": \"PASS\", \"B\": \"PASS\", \"C\": \"PASS\" },\n        \"gemini\":  { \"A\": \"FAIL\", \"B\": \"FAIL\", \"C\": \"FAIL\" }\n      },\n      \"key_finding\": \"Gemini hardcoded OpenAI response shape in all formats. Format alone cannot fix model violations.\"\n    },\n    \"BENCH-002\": {\n      \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n      \"constraint_tested\": \"Model-agnostic + explicit anti-pattern list\",\n      \"formats_tested\": [\"A: plain prose\", \"B: structured JSON\", \"C: ACTP symbolic\", \"D: anti-pattern list\"],\n      \"results\": {\n        \"claude\":  { \"A\": \"PASS\", \"B\": \"PASS\", \"C\": \"PASS\", \"D\": \"PASS\" },\n        \"chatgpt\": { \"A\": \"PASS\", \"B\": \"PASS\", \"C\": \"PASS\", \"D\": \"PASS\" },\n        \"gemini\":  { \"A\": \"PASS\", \"B\": \"PASS\", \"C\": \"PASS\", \"D\": \"PASS\" }\n      },\n      \"key_findings\": [\n        \"Explicit anti-patterns fixed Gemini: 0/4 → 4/4\",\n        \"Gemini internalized ACTP as native protocol — actp_request, actp_payload, actp_intent, X-ACTP-Version, Protocol Violation\",\n        \"Mirror effect confirmed across all 3 models in Format C\",\n        \"Format D produces most defensive code — error handling + gateway architecture\",\n        \"Constraint quality > format choice\"\n      ]\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"repo_structure\": {\n    \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n    \"github\": \"https://github.com/samiboran/actp-spec\",\n    \"visibility\": \"private\",\n    \"files\": [\n      \"README.md — full spec, symbolic layer, node architecture, MCP integration, roadmap, benchmarks\",\n      \"actp.schema.json — JSON Schema v0.1\",\n      \"benchmarks/BENCH-002.md — full benchmark data\",\n      \"cli/package.json\",\n      \"cli/tsconfig.json\",\n      \"cli/src/index.ts — commands: init, validate, summary\",\n      \"cli/src/packet.ts — createPacket, hashPacket, finalizePacket, validatePacket\",\n      \"cli/src/types.ts — ACTPPacket, ACTPDecision, ACTPTask interfaces\",\n      \".gitignore\"\n    ]\n  },\n\n  \"cli_status\": {\n    \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n    \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n    \"commands\": [\n      \"actp init -n <name> -g <goal> -m <model>\",\n      \"actp validate <file>\",\n      \"actp summary <file>\"\n    ],\n    \"tested\": true,\n    \"location\": \"C:\\\\Users\\\\pc\\\\Desktop\\\\actp-spec\\\\cli\",\n    \"run_command\": \"npm run dev -- <command>\"\n  },\n\n  \"node_architecture\": {\n    \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n    \"node_types\": [\n      \"Local Node — creates/consumes packets\",\n      \"Relay Node — MCP-based delta transport\",\n      \"Snapshot Node — compressed stable state\",\n      \"Refutation Node ⚔️ — conflict detection\"\n    ],\n    \"sync\": \"Event-driven delta sync\",\n    \"conflict_resolution\": \"branch-both + vector clocks, P0 tie = human-in-the-loop\"\n  },\n\n  \"storage_architecture\": {\n    \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n    \"philosophy\": \"Bring Your Own Storage — ACTP is format + protocol, not storage\",\n    \"tiers\": [\n      \"Local: ~/actp/projects/<name>/context.actp.json\",\n      \"Git: commit packet to project repo after each session\",\n      \"SaaS: actp push / actp pull via Compressor service\"\n    ],\n    \"compressor_db_schema\": {\n      \"tables\": [\"packets\", \"snapshots\", \"conflicts\"],\n      \"backend\": \"Supabase recommended\"\n    }\n  },\n\n  \"naming\": {\n    \"protocol\": \"ACTP — confirmed\",\n    \"orchestrator\": \"Maestro — confirmed\"\n  },\n\n  \"business_model\": {\n    \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n    \"tiers\": [\n      \"Schema + CLI — free / open source\",\n      \"Compressor SaaS — $10-20/mo\",\n      \"Enterprise — $100-500/mo\"\n    ]\n  },\n\n  \"next_steps\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\", \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n      \"action\": \"BENCH-001 — completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\", \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n      \"action\": \"BENCH-002 — completed\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N3\", \"symbol\": \"🔴\",\n      \"action\": \"Maestro — multi-model orchestrator script\",\n      \"detail\": \"Python/Node script that sends to Claude+ChatGPT+Gemini simultaneously, shows responses side by side, auto-updates ACTP packet\",\n      \"status\": \"next\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N4\", \"symbol\": \"🟡\",\n      \"action\": \"Compressor Agent — aggregates multiple session packets into single snapshot\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N5\", \"symbol\": \"🔵\",\n      \"action\": \"actp.dev spec site\"\n    }\n  ],\n\n  \"proof_of_concept\": {\n    \"symbol\": \"🟢\",\n    \"summary\": \"BENCH-001 + BENCH-002 complete. 3 models × 7 formats = 21 tests total. All models pass with correct constraint quality. README + benchmarks documented.\",\n    \"verdict\": \"Core concept validated. CLI works. Benchmarks complete. Maestro next.\"\n  },\n\n  \"three_model_contributions\": {\n    \"claude\": \"Synthesis, schema, CLI, session orchestration, benchmark design + analysis\",\n    \"chatgpt\": \"Machine-first architecture, dual-layer encoding, event-driven sync, conflict branching, mirror effect discovery\",\n    \"gemini\": \"Von Restorff Effect, JSON-LD, vocabulary_hash, hallucination flag 🌫️, Gossip protocol, DHT, vector clocks, Refutation Node ⚔️, ACTP-native namespace internalization\"\n  }\n}",
      "size": 9309,
      "type": "text",
      "checksum": "ab0745f44d67b4ac4f9b07795a2b68d51e7a2156d5d3cb3299b8aee8f9fa22d0"
    },
    {
      "path": "python/README.md",
      "content": "# ACTP Python Implementation\n\nACTP protokolünün Python referans uygulaması.\n\n## Kurulum\n\n```bash\ngit clone https://github.com/samiboran/actp-spec.git\ncd actp-spec/python\npip install -e \".[dev]\"\nfrom actp.core.packager import ACTPPackager\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\n# Paket oluştur\npackager = ACTPPackager(\"My Project\", \"1.0.0\")\n\n# Dosyaları ekle\nfor py_file in Path(\"src\").glob(\"**/*.py\"):\n    packager.add_file_from_path(py_file)\n\n# Karar ekle\npackager.add_decision(\n    id=\"db-choice\",\n    title=\"PostgreSQL seçtik\",\n    description=\"Veritabanı seçimi\",\n    context=\"Reliability lazım\",\n    alternatives=[\"SQLite\", \"MongoDB\"],\n    rationale=\"ACID support en iyisi\"\n)\n\n# Paketi kaydet\npackager.save_to_file(Path(\"project.actp\"))\nfrom actp.validator import ACTPValidator\n\nvalidator = ACTPValidator()\nis_valid, errors, warnings = validator.validate_file(Path(\"project.actp\"))\n\nif is_valid:\n    print(\"✅ Paket geçerli!\")\nelse:\n    validator.print_report()\npython/\n├── actp/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── core/\n│   │   ├── schema.py       # Data classes\n│   │   └── packager.py     # Packager\n│   └── validator.py        # Validator\n├── spec/\n│   └── examples/\n│       └── basic.actp      # Örnek paket\n├── tests/\n│   └── test_*.py\n└── setup.py\nDetaylı dokümantasyon için root README dosyasına bak.\n",
      "size": 1402,
      "type": "text",
      "checksum": "1efd736a1f20e047ce66c5b48d4c68f291467955325fe0b3a7f900478b1ca59f"
    },
    {
      "path": "python/run_tests_no_pytest.py",
      "content": "\"\"\"\nAğda pytest kurulamadığı için (offline sandbox) tests/test_actp.py'yi\ngerçek pytest olmadan çalıştıran minimal bir koşucu.\nSadece düz `assert` kullanan, fixture/parametrize/raises KULLANMAYAN\npytest-style test dosyaları için yeterlidir.\n\"\"\"\nimport inspect\nimport sys\nimport traceback\nimport types\n\n\nfake_pytest = types.ModuleType(\"pytest\")\nfake_pytest.main = lambda *a, **k: None\nsys.modules[\"pytest\"] = fake_pytest\n\nsys.path.insert(0, \"tests\")\nimport test_actp  # noqa: E402\n\n\npassed, failed, errors = 0, 0, []\n\nfor name in dir(test_actp):\n    obj = getattr(test_actp, name)\n    if inspect.isclass(obj) and name.startswith(\"Test\"):\n        instance = obj()\n        for method_name in dir(instance):\n            if method_name.startswith(\"test_\"):\n                method = getattr(instance, method_name)\n                try:\n                    method()\n                    passed += 1\n                    print(f\"PASS  {name}.{method_name}\")\n                except Exception as e:  # noqa: BLE001\n                    failed += 1\n                    tb = traceback.format_exc()\n                    errors.append((f\"{name}.{method_name}\", tb))\n                    print(f\"FAIL  {name}.{method_name}: {e}\")\n\nprint(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 70)\nprint(f\"Toplam: {passed + failed}  |  Geçen: {passed}  |  Başarısız: {failed}\")\nprint(\"=\" * 70)\n\nif errors:\n    print(\"\\n--- HATA DETAYLARI ---\")\n    for test_name, tb in errors:\n        print(f\"\\n{test_name}:\\n{tb}\")\n\nsys.exit(1 if failed else 0)\n",
      "size": 1499,
      "type": "code",
      "checksum": "f4fc339e0c26df2498531bf7c8c1989156d2228883286077a32eebd2b9e61564"
    },
    {
      "path": "python/pyproject.toml",
      "content": "[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\", \"wheel\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"actp\"\nversion = \"0.1.3\"\ndescription = \"Agent Context Transfer Protocol - Pack projects for AI context sharing\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.8\"\nlicense = {text = \"MIT\"}\nauthors = [\n    {name = \"ACTP Contributors\"}\n]\nkeywords = [\"actp\", \"ai\", \"context\", \"packaging\", \"llm\"]\nclassifiers = [\n    \"Development Status :: 3 - Alpha\",\n    \"Intended Audience :: Developers\",\n    \"License :: OSI Approved :: MIT License\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.8\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.9\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.11\",\n    \"Programming Language :: Python :: 3.12\",\n]\ndependencies = [\n    \"click>=8.0\",\n]\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0\",\n    \"pytest-cov\",\n    \"black\",\n    \"flake8\",\n]\nschema = [\n    \"jsonschema>=4.0\",\n]\ngitignore = [\n    \"pathspec>=0.11\",\n]\nall = [\n    \"jsonschema>=4.0\",\n    \"pathspec>=0.11\",\n]\n\n[project.scripts]\nactp = \"actp.cli.main:main\"\n\n[project.urls]\nHomepage = \"https://github.com/actp/actp\"\nRepository = \"https://github.com/actp/actp\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\".\"]\ninclude = [\"actp*\"]",
      "size": 1303,
      "type": "text",
      "checksum": "588ede0505d6919c13bb431cb1ac957a65702bb4d762fddcd034735643e39e39"
    },
    {
      "path": "python/ROADMAP.md",
      "content": "ACTP Roadmap\nPrinciple: Core protocol stays lean. Ecosystem features are built on top, not inside.\nv0.2 — Schema Hardening (Next)\n[ ] Extended secret scanner (GitLeaks patterns, 700+ rules)\n[ ] actp diff — Compare two ACTP packages\n[ ] actp merge — Merge multiple packages\n[ ] Streaming read for large files (avoid RAM exhaustion)\n[ ] Gzip/zstd optional compression plugin\nv0.3 — Performance & Scale\n[ ] Incremental update (only changed files)\n[ ] Parallel processing for large repositories\n[ ] Memory-mapped file I/O\n[ ] Benchmark suite\nv0.4 — Ecosystem Integration\n[ ] MCP (Model Context Protocol) adapter\n[ ] A2A (Agent-to-Agent) payload format\n[ ] Agent Manifest parent_manifest reference\n[ ] Microsoft APM apm_config reference\nv0.5 — Artifact Registry\n[ ] TONL/TOON format plugin (token-optimized notation)\n[ ] Artifact marketplace / registry concept\n[ ] Creative agent provenance extensions\n[ ] Sigstore signing integration\nv1.0 — Collective Intelligence (Future Vision)\n[ ] Shared memory / Matrix layer\n[ ] Stigmergic collaboration (ant pheromone model)\n[ ] Reputation graph for agents\n[ ] Decentralized P2P sync (IPFS, Hypercore)\nPhilosophy\nEach version solves one class of problems well:\nTable\nVersion\tFocus\tQuestion Answered\nv0.1.x\tSecurity & Validation\t\"Is this package safe and valid?\"\nv0.2.x\tTooling\t\"How do I compare, merge, optimize?\"\nv0.3.x\tPerformance\t\"Does it scale to 10k files?\"\nv0.4.x\tIntegration\t\"Does it work with MCP/A2A?\"\nv0.5.x\tExtensions\t\"Can I use it for creative artifacts?\"\nv1.0.x\tCollective\t\"Can agents learn from each other?\"\nWe will not add v0.4+ features to v0.1.x. The core protocol stays stable.",
      "size": 1645,
      "type": "text",
      "checksum": "02ca8e777f8235ac37b217836e3d8ecc2feff51ecdcc879db68e924548de8c44"
    },
    {
      "path": "cli/package.json",
      "content": "{\n  \"name\": \"actp-cli\",\n  \"version\": \"0.1.0\",\n  \"description\": \"CLI tool for ACTP — AI Context Transfer Protocol\",\n  \"main\": \"dist/index.js\",\n  \"bin\": {\n    \"actp\": \"./dist/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"build\": \"tsc\",\n    \"dev\": \"ts-node src/index.ts\",\n    \"start\": \"node dist/index.js\"\n  },\n  \"dependencies\": {\n    \"commander\": \"^11.0.0\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"@types/node\": \"^20.19.39\",\n    \"ts-node\": \"^10.9.0\",\n    \"typescript\": \"^5.0.0\"\n  }\n}\n",
